# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the working
# tree to CRLF at checkout. That is not cosmetic here: `templates/` is the
# source of truth the asset installer copies verbatim, and `doctor` verifies
# installed assets by SHA-256 against the bundled template. A CRLF checkout
# therefore produces different asset hashes on Windows than on Linux for the
# same released version, and the published npm tarball (built from the
# committed LF bytes) would match neither.
* text=auto eol=lf
